@startuml metadata_runtime_directory_mapping
title Metadata to CampusAgent Runtime Directory

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 9e7cc8952937a697fe2c16ff0de287b32bc4c891):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/agent/FileAgentDirectoryResolver.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/agent/RuntimeAgentPromptLoader.java.
' Observed behavior: pi and pi-mono-java discover Skill metadata from SKILL.md frontmatter.
' Observed behavior: the Runtime reads one controlled Agent directory directly and does not cache it.
' Observed behavior: HTTP V1 reads agent/{agent_id}/.campusclaw while retaining its existing filenames.
' Observed behavior: RuntimeSessionStore persists Session state in a shared database.
' Observed behavior: RuntimeApiConstants still accepts agent_ plus 24 alphanumeric characters.
' Architecture change: Agent, Tool, and Skill IDs use typed prefixes plus 32 hex UUID characters.
' Design reason: align Runtime identifiers with the metadata authority and reject untyped aliases.
' Target-only design: a future metadata compiler may publish the controlled Agent directory.
' Design reason: keep Agent-specific disclosure local while Managers remain runtime authorities.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam file {
  BackgroundColor #F0FDF4
  BorderColor #16A34A
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

rectangle "Resolved metadata input" as Input {
  rectangle "AGENT\nid, version, system_prompt\nbinding_models, bindings, policy" as AgentMetadata
  rectangle "SKILL\nname, description, content\nskill and tool bindings" as SkillMetadata
  rectangle "TOOL\nid, name, description\nschema, source, permission" as ToolMetadata
}

rectangle "Runtime bundle compiler" as Compiler {
  rectangle "Validate versions, IDs,\ndependency closure,\ncase-fold conflicts and policy" as Validate
  rectangle "Render prompt and\nSkill resources" as Render
  rectangle "Publish Agent directory\natomically" as Publish
}

rectangle "Controlled Agent directory\ncase-sensitive file system\nagent/<agent-id>/.campusclaw/" as AgentDirectory {
  file "settings.json\ndefaultModel, enabledModels" as SettingsFile
  file "SYSTEM.md\nAgent instructions\nDirect Agent tool summaries" as SystemFile
  file "skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\nFrontmatter and Skill content" as SkillFile
  file "skills/<skill-name>/references/tools.json\nDirect Skill tool summaries" as SkillToolsFile
}

database "Agent metadata authority\nAgent model and binding policy" as AgentAuthority
database "Tool Manager authority\nTool schema, status,\npermission and execution" as ToolManager
database "Model Manager authority\nModel descriptor,\nallowlist and invocation" as ModelManager
database "RuntimeSessionStore\nSession, current-branch Entry,\ninternal execution state and revisions" as SessionStore

AgentMetadata --> Validate
SkillMetadata --> Validate
ToolMetadata --> Validate
Validate --> Render
Render --> Publish
Publish --> SettingsFile : identity, version and binding_models
Publish --> SystemFile : system_prompt and direct tools
Publish --> SkillFile : name, description and content
Publish --> SkillToolsFile : direct Skill tools

AgentMetadata ..> AgentAuthority : publish metadata
ToolMetadata ..> ToolManager : publish executable definition
SettingsFile ..> ModelManager : model selection snapshot
AgentMetadata ..> ModelManager : authoritative model bindings
AgentDirectory ..> SessionStore : resolved working directory

note right of SkillToolsFile
Only tool_id, name and description.
Schemas stay in Tool Manager.
Child Skill tools are not merged.
end note

note left of AgentDirectory
agent_id = agent- + 32 hex UUID characters
tool_id = tool- + 32 hex UUID characters
skill_id = skill- + 32 hex UUID characters
UUID payloads contain no hyphens.
Compare IDs byte-for-byte.
Reject Agent ID case-fold collisions.
Verify the directory and file boundary.
end note

note right of SettingsFile
defaultModel must be present in enabledModels.
enabledModels is a non-empty explicit allowlist.
Model Manager still revalidates every selection and invocation.
end note
@enduml
